       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no listed allergies, so nothing in the chart explains a higher dose. A dose this high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT effects, GI and bleeding effects, and seizures, and it has no established added benefit.\n\nCan you tell me which of these applies?\n\n- **Dose error:** You may have meant 40 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily. Typical dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg and titrates up to a maximum of 200 mg.\n- **Intentional supratherapeutic dose:** If you want 400 mg for a specific reason, give me the dose and a short rationale. I'll enter it with a note such as \"dose exceeds labeled max, intentional per attending\", and pharmacy may still want to verify it.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
